<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Alamut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1256">1256</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alamut">Alamut</a> was the capture of the mountain fortress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismaili-state">Nizari Ismailis</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> by Mongol forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a> in 1256. It ended the Nizari Ismaili state. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> place the event at the start of Hulagu's campaign that led to the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-alamut.jpg" alt="Siege of Alamut" width="275" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Basawan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Assassins2-alamut.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Hulagu destroyed the Nizari Ismaili state in 1256, securing the surrender of its imam and, after the <b>Siege of Alamut</b>, the fortress itself, then advanced into Mesopotamia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
